player: synchronize restored video with already-running audio

Disabling video resets the A/V delay without emptying the audio output.
When video is selected again, audio can still have several seconds queued.
The first video frame is shown immediately in STATUS_SYNCING, but the next
one is scheduled against that old audio backlog and a near-zero delay,
freezing the first picture for the backlog's duration.

Initialize the existing delay invariant from the written audio timestamp
and the first video timestamp when only video is restarting. Ordinary
loads/seeks synchronize audio separately and keep the existing path.

diff --git a/player/video.c b/player/video.c
--- a/player/video.c
+++ b/player/video.c
@@ -376,6 +376,20 @@ static void handle_new_frame(struct MPContext *mpctx)
     double pts = mpctx->next_frames[0]->pts;
     bool is_sparse = mpctx->vo_chain && mpctx->vo_chain->is_sparse;
 
+    // A video-only restart preserves the AO's queued audio, but resets delay.
+    // Rejoin its timeline once, when the first video timestamp becomes known:
+    // delay is the media time written past this frame, not just audio written
+    // since the video chain was rebuilt. Full seeks/loads also restart audio
+    // and perform their synchronization in the audio startup path instead.
+    if (mpctx->video_status == STATUS_SYNCING &&
+        mpctx->video_pts == MP_NOPTS_VALUE &&
+        mpctx->audio_status == STATUS_PLAYING && pts != MP_NOPTS_VALUE)
+    {
+        double a_pts = written_audio_pts(mpctx);
+        if (a_pts != MP_NOPTS_VALUE)
+            mpctx->delay = a_pts + mpctx->opts->audio_delay - pts;
+    }
+
     if (mpctx->video_pts != MP_NOPTS_VALUE) {
         frame_time = pts - mpctx->video_pts;
         double tolerance = mpctx->demuxer->ts_resets_possible &&
